Z||000003||olliver||11-01-2001||07:42 PM||||I think it's safe to say that at this point I am the expert on this subject.  With all the freaking gremlins i'm having with my rebuild, i've researched this subject enough that i could write a thesis on it.<P>I don't live in ontario anymore (thank heavens) but i just got my injectors rebuilt here in edmonton.  When i removed the injectors from my engine, i noticed that two of them were different.  They didn't have the cap on the ends.  The tips of them were a cylinder and if you looked up inside you could see 6 tiny pin holes for the fuel.  I called the dealership and was told that they are acceptable replacements.  But when i shipped them off to the injector rebuild shop, he told me that they were going to be problems as soon as he seen them.  Aparently hen he first applied fuel pressure, they just pissed out like a garden hose.  He said that he had to make multiple adjustments until he could get them to mist properly.  Well long story short, he sold me two proper injectors (like the other 4) rebuilt my other 4 for only $200.00 That's a far better deal than $99.00/ea i was quoted at the local u.a.p./napa dealers.<P>The name of the shop is:<BR>Duke's Injector Service<BR>Spruce Grove, AB<BR>(780) 960-3388<P>P.S. It only took him an afternoon to rebuild my injectors.<P>Olliver||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||11-01-2001||07:50 PM||||luckily, I have a 85gt and 87GT, I will pull my 85GT's injectors, have them rebuilt then put them in my 87GT when they come back, and send the 87's out.<P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  The place to go for Fiero INFO! <BR>Home of my 87 GT and 85 GT<BR>Justin C.<BR>Engineer, Designer and<BR>Technical Trainer for Nortel Networks Business Products.||||reg||1
